  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Strengthened Migration Governance Frameworks for Sustainable Development in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration dynamics in Angola have drastically changed in recent years, resulting in an increasingly complex landscape of challenges and opportunities stemming from human mobility. The objective of this project is to contribute to strengthening evidence-based migration governance through the Migration Governance Indicators (MGI) assessment and targeted policy capacity building in Angola. The intended outcome is that the Government of Angola will identify key aspects of its migration governance framework to be further strengthened to respond to new migration dynamics in the country. To achieve this Outcome, two Outputs are planned. Under Output 1.1, the central Government institutions, through the Ministry of Home Affairs, will receive evidence through an MGI assessment to revise Angola&#x2019;s National Migration Policy, rooted in the GCM and based on best gender-sensitive practices from other countries, through a whole-of-government and whole-of-society approach. Under Output 1.2, Government officials will be trained on the technical capacities and know-how on key emerging issues that will be central in the development of their migration policies by piloting IOM&apos;s new Essentials of Migration Policymaking training. Through these two outputs, the Government of Angola will have a better understanding of which aspects of its migration governance framework could be further strengthened to respond to current (new) migration dynamics in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
